+# State at this continuation
+
+## Original invariant objects
+
+One G(R) construction, its represented e and external tau; the infinite arithmetic quotient; g=2xi; full packet multiplicities; the same theta maps, remainder matrices, source norms, canonical G_N, and operator A=M_S. No metric or arithmetic Taylor unit is replaced.
+
+## What is now calculated
+
+1. The SGA finite-flat trace on the exact cyclic packet, its diagonal coevaluation, trace radical, and all degrees of its periodic diagonal resolution.
+2. The determinant of the prior exponential period matrix, with its complete monomial constant and ray orientation.
+3. Recovery of the cyclic spectrum, including multiplicities, from the full coefficient-direction determinant derivatives.
+4. The explicit transport of the original metric/control to period coordinates; all common period determinant factors in endpoint ratios are known and cancel exactly.
+5. An invariant constituent's period minor and logarithmic derivative, giving the original aggregate spectral defect. Its first possible normal acceleration is the specified rank-one parameter correction.
+
+## What has not been inferred
+
+Finite-field weight-one purity for the auxiliary exponential sheaf has not been identified with a bound on the original A or canonical theta Gram. Evaluating a full determinant alone does not bound its individual singular values or proper exterior minors. The trace response through the retained diagonal is not a positivity theorem for the original sesquilinear Weil form.
+
